  "baseline": "Native CPU 490718 cached arrays; the two affected incoming native ionization, density, emissivity and thermal fields were reloaded at each epoch. Independent tests call public compute_ionization_field with only the conditional table and history stages replaced. The initial node uses the native empty previous box. No lightcone run.",
  "calculation": "The native setup clips current and previous density, measures the unclipped extrema, and pads each density axis by 0.001. It clips turnover grids and supplies the original per-radius mass upper/conditioning limit. The GPU builds current population tables at the current growth, and previous tables at the previous growth, using the same current scaling constants and current filtered turnover fields. Previous tables are built only if the previous unconditional ACG+MCG Nion > 1e-4. Kernel applies native bilinear log-table interpolation and per-species saturation, casts the corrected history to float32 before final upper clipping and uses these stored results for the two double volume means. The consumer reads independent history planes [radius,index].",
  "residency": "GPU table results are retained through per-radius lookup; the CUDA callback does not write those tables to native arrays or transfer them back to the device.",
  "scope_limit": "The validated case is a cubic mass-dependent E-integral atomic+molecular run, photoheating on, GL or adaptive table code (this fully integrated history test uses GL). The endpoint-safe lookup evaluates a terminal table knot using its left interval and explicitly checks out-of-range inputs. This test leaves FFT filtering and excursion barrier native.",
